@startuml
title Sequence diagram: who is told when an event is rejected
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API are numbered, as in the draw.io and PDF
' versions.
' A notification is a record saved in PostgreSQL when the event is rejected. Nothing is
' pushed to its recipient (no email, websocket or polling): the Web App fetches it
' later with GET /api/notifications.

actor "Event\nOrganiser" as organiser
actor "Venue\nStaff" as venue
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Later, the Web App fetches each recipient's saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
organiser -> web : Open notifications
autonumber
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : Your event request was rejected, with the reason
autonumber stop
web --> organiser : Show notifications

venue -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : A venue booking or hold was released
autonumber stop
web --> venue : Show notifications
@enduml
